flowchart TB
  accTitle: Cognitive cycle graph routing
  accDescr: The cognitive graph moves from initialization and interpretation to context and evidence, workspace and planning, recovery and governance, authorization and execution, then observation and learning. Clarification, evidence, planning, human control, approval, and memory update create conditional loops or interruptions. Terminal paths are completion and escalation.
  START([Start]) --> INIT[Initialize]
  INIT --> INT[Interpret]
  INT -->|ready| CTX[Load context]
  INT -->|clarification| CLAR[Await clarification]
  CLAR --> INT
  INT -->|unknown or out of scope| ESC[Escalate]
  CTX --> UNC[Assess uncertainty]
  UNC --> RET[Retrieve evidence]
  RET -->|more evidence| EVID[Await evidence]
  EVID --> CTX
  RET -->|blocked| B2[B2 recovery]
  B2 -->|reconsider| CTX
  RET -->|usable| WS[B3 workspace]
  WS --> PROP[Propose candidates]
  PROP --> EVAL[Evaluate candidates]
  EVAL -->|retry or evidence| PROP
  EVAL -->|selected| B4[B4 intention]
  B4 --> B6[B6 meta-control]
  B6 -->|re-propose| PROP
  B6 -->|human decision| HUMAN[Await human control]
  HUMAN --> B6
  B6 -->|authorize| AUTH[Authorize candidate]
  AUTH -->|approval needed| APPROVE[Await exact approval]
  APPROVE --> REVALIDATE[Revalidate plan and approval]
  AUTH -->|pre-authorized| REVALIDATE
  REVALIDATE -->|current| EXEC[Execute authorized action]
  REVALIDATE -->|stale or new evidence| CTX
  EXEC --> OBS[Observe and reconcile]
  OBS --> WM[Update working memory]
  WM --> LEARN[Record outcome episode]
  LEARN --> COMPLETE([Complete])
  OBS -->|conflict or reload| CTX
  B6 -->|stop or unsafe| ESC
  ESC --> END([End])
  COMPLETE --> END
